{"assets":["/statement-assets/35852fb9bdee72940760abf239076d25bcd03a11f03abbac5ec08bc16fb0224d.png","/statement-assets/eef6b108fa1f9207e5b67f13dece3fe62dcbc09265bf5e4ffd7a6244e885822e.png","/statement-assets/90886cbdd562b5b41d05b2e3071a6e27e6eddca88146d2e59c96a81826428357.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"754","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Dasha and cyclic table"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"6 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Dasha is fond of challenging puzzles: Rubik's Cube "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 × 3 × 3"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4 × 4 × 4"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5 × 5 × 5"},{"kind":"text","text":" and so on. This time she has a cyclic table of size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":", and each cell of the table contains a lowercase English letter. Each cell has coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i, j)"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ i < n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ j < m"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The table is cyclic means that to the right of cell "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i, j)"},{"kind":"text","text":" there is the cell "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/35852fb9bdee72940760abf239076d25bcd03a11f03abbac5ec08bc16fb0224d.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", and to the down there is the cell "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/eef6b108fa1f9207e5b67f13dece3fe62dcbc09265bf5e4ffd7a6244e885822e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Dasha has a pattern as well. A pattern is a non-cyclic table of size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r × c"},{"kind":"text","text":". Each cell is either a lowercase English letter or a question mark. Each cell has coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i, j)"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ i < r"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ j < c"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The goal of the puzzle is to find all the appearance positions of the pattern in the cyclic table."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We say that the cell "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i, j)"},{"kind":"text","text":" of cyclic table is an appearance position, if for every pair "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ x < r"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ y < c"},{"kind":"text","text":" one of the following conditions holds: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" There is a question mark in the cell "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the pattern, or "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The cell "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/90886cbdd562b5b41d05b2e3071a6e27e6eddca88146d2e59c96a81826428357.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the cyclic table equals to the cell "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the pattern. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Dasha solved this puzzle in no time, as well as all the others she ever tried. Can you solve it?."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, m ≤ 400"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the cyclic table sizes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains a string of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lowercase English characters — the description of the cyclic table."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ r, c ≤ 400"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the sizes of the pattern."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains a string of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"c"},{"kind":"text","text":" lowercase English letter and/or characters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' — the description of the pattern."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines. Each of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines should contain "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters. Each of the characters should equal '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' or '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th character of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":"-indexed) line should be equal to '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', in case the cell "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i, j)"},{"kind":"text","text":" is an appearance position, otherwise it should be equal to '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 7\nqcezchs\nhhedywq\nwikywqy\nqckrqzt\nbqexcxz\n3 2\n??\nyw\n?q\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0000100\n0001001\n0000000\n0000000\n0000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10 10\nfwtoayylhw\nyyaryyjawr\nywrdzwhscy\nhnsyyxiphn\nbnjwzyyjvo\nkkjgseenwn\ngvmiflpcsy\nlxvkwrobwu\nwyybbcocyy\nyysijsvqry\n2 2\n??\nyy\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","te